# Lights every dot-matrix pixel and every status indicator on the
# PC-1500A's LCD at once, for visually checking LCDDisplayView's
# indicator/dot-matrix sizing (plan.md Phase 2a "LOG panel" work)
# against real hardware. See lcdallon_1500a.asm's own header for the
# full background, display-RAM layout, and BREAK-poll details.
#
# post-load-keys runs `CALL &7C01,X` automatically -- safe even though
# the routine loops until BREAK (ON) is pressed and never returns
# during loading: every preset step (a bounded runCycles() call, per
# PC1500PresetLoader.cpp) still terminates on its own cycle budget
# regardless of what the CPU is doing, it just leaves the CPU parked
# inside the routine's own wait loop once the preset finishes applying
# -- exactly the state this preset wants to hand the app: display
# already fully lit, waiting only for BREAK.
#
# After this preset loads, in the running app: everything is already
# lit -- just press ON (BREAK) when done looking, to return to the
# READY prompt.
model: PC-1500A

keys:
  - key: cl
  - type: NEW0
  - key: mode

program:
  path: lcdallon_1500a.bin
  format: binary
  address: 0x7C01

keys:
  - type: CALL&7C01,X
